# 2. Secured and Monitored Web Infrastructure

This setup adds HTTPS, firewalls, and monitoring.

## Components
- **SSL (HTTPS)**: secure communication between users and servers.
- **Firewalls**: filter traffic, only allow necessary ports (e.g. 80, 443, 3306).
- **Monitoring**: agents collect metrics (QPS, errors, CPU, etc.).
- **DB Replication**: primary + replica for redundancy.

## Diagram

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  U["User"] --> D["DNS (www.foobar.com)"]
  D --> LB["HAProxy Load Balancer (HTTPS)"]
  LB --> FW1["Firewall #1"]
  LB --> W1["Web+App Server #1"]
  LB --> W2["Web+App Server #2"]
  W1 --> FW2["Firewall #2"]
  W2 --> FW2
  FW2 --> DB1["MySQL Primary"]
  DB1 --> FW3["Firewall #3"]
  FW3 --> DB2["MySQL Replica"]
  W1 --> MON["Monitoring Agent"]
  W2 --> MON
  DB1 --> MON
```

## Notes
- HTTPS prevents eavesdropping.
- Firewalls enforce least-privilege rules.
- Monitoring improves reliability by detecting failures.
- Still one active DB (replica is read-only).
